manifold_riemannian,流形对齐与黎曼几何 (Manifold Alignment & Riemannian Geometry),manifold alignment Riemannian geometry deep learning NeurIPS ICML 2024 2025,3,NeurIPS Poster T-REGS: Minimum Spanning Tree Regularization for Self-Supervised Learning,https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/116424,neurips.cc,0.9976404,"uniformity on arbitrary compact Riemannian manifolds. Several experiments on synthetic data and on classical SSL benchmarks validate the effectiveness of our approach at enhancing representation quality. [...] Self-supervised learning (SSL) has emerged as a powerful paradigm for learning representations without labeled data, often by enforcing invariance to input transformations such as rotations or blurring. Recent studies have highlighted two pivotal properties for effective representations: (i) avoiding dimensional collapse-where the learned features occupy only a low-dimensional subspace, and (ii) enhancing uniformity of the induced distribution. In this work, we introduce T-REGS, a simple regularization framework for SSL based on the length of the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) over the learned representation. We provide theoretical analysis demonstrating that T-REGS simultaneously mitigates dimensional collapse and promotes distribution uniformity on arbitrary compact Riemannian manifolds. [...] Skip to yearly menu bar

