manifold_riemannian,流形对齐与黎曼几何 (Manifold Alignment & Riemannian Geometry),Riemannian optimization deep learning alignment transfer learning 2024 2025,3,Deep Neural Networks Inspired by Differential Equations,https://arxiv.org/html/2510.09685v1,arxiv.org,0.9964619,"al., 2024), and Statistical Flow Matching (SFM) (Cheng et al., 2024) bring in information geometry, aligning probability transport with natural statistical metrics such as the Fisher–Rao distance. Diffeomorphism Conditional Flow Matching (DiffeoCFM) (Collas et al., 2025) further extends flow matching to positive-definite matrix manifolds via pullback geometry. Altogether, these innovations substantially broaden the applicability and expressivity of flow matching, providing a robust geometric foundation for flow-based generative modeling in complex domains. [...] which facilitates the direct generation of samples with specified attributes to ensure alignment with conditioning information. This capability is particularly beneficial for tasks such as class-conditional image synthesis.

Discrete Flow Matching (DFM) (Campbell et al., 2022; Gat et al., 2024) generalizes flow matching to discrete and categorical data domains by replacing the continuous flow with a continuous-time Markov jump process. The dynamics are governed by a time-dependent rate matrix Qθ​(t)Q\_{\theta}(t):

