(2) a text encoder gφ : C →Z, with parameters φ, which maps a caption c to a feature vector zc = gφ(c). [...] largely limit the plasticity of the model during continual learning, and we therefore 4 Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025 man in blue wetsuit is surfing on wave Text encoder Image encoder CLIP loss Dm-1 Dm W A B image-text pairs Text or Image encoder contrastive knowledge consolidation Figure 2: Illustration of the C-CLIP model. We make two adjustments to CLIP: (1) applying LoRA to reduce forgetting, though it slightly hampers new task learning; (2) introducing contrastive knowl-edge consolidation (CKC) improves learning on new tasks and reduces forgetting. This combination significantly enhances the continual learning ability of CLIP, achieving downstream task perfor-mance that matches or exceeds full fine-tuning and preserving its general zero-shot ability. [...] Regarding learning rates, we tested several values. For COCO-caption, we set the learning rate for the text encoder to 80 times that of the image encoder, while for other datasets, it was set to 10 times.
16 Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025 The base learning rate was 5e-7 for COCO-caption, 1e-5 for Flickr30K, and 3e-5 for other datasets, from Pet to Sketch. Our method’s code will be open-sourced, and further details can be found in the released code.",True
