### Abstract [...] In this work, we address the test-time adaptation challenge in graph neural networks (GNNs), focusing on overcoming the limitations in flexibility and generalization inherent in existing data-centric approaches. To this end, we propose a novel research problem, test-time graph neural dataset search, which seeks to learn a parameterized test-time graph distribution to enhance the inference performance of unseen test graphs on well-trained GNNs. Specifically, we propose a generative Projection based test-time Graph Neural Dataset Search method, named PGNDS, which maps the unseen test graph distribution back to the known training distribution through a generation process guided by well-trained GNNs. The proposed PGNDS framework consists of three key modules: (1) dual conditional diffusion",True
